# Correlation dimension D_f of the fibril cross-section versus surface-diffusion parameter T_s
# Columns: T_s   D_f (correlation dimension, raw)   SE over seeds
# Seeds per T_s: 2: 15, 8: 15, 16: 40, 32: 5, 64: 5, 128: 5, 512: 5, 1024: 5, 4096: 15, 8192: 15
# Periodic cylinders (period 216, nb = 60000), 12 sections per cylinder, ~5000 molecules per section.
# D_f = slope of log C(r) vs log r for 4 <= r <= R_bar/3; C(r) = fraction of point pairs at distance <= r.
# No boundary correction; a uniform disc with the same n and R_bar gives 1.93-1.95 in this window.
# Source: Reviews/N18_df_ten_ts/df_periodic_summary.csv (corr_primary_mean, _se). Use a logarithmic x axis.
